From: Plain Browser
Subject: [ui] Settings > Privacy and security: the list of sites with protections off

Category: 60-ui. A section under "Site settings" on chrome://settings/privacy lists
plainbrowser.shields.exceptions (the per-site exception list, registered through 20-hooks) with a remove button per site
and an Add dialog. The element is new (privacy_page/plainbrowser_shields_exceptions.*, a Lit element like the
page around it; Chromium is moving Settings off Polymer) and edits the pref through settingsPrivate, which needs
the pref in prefs_util.cc's allowlist. Entries are stored as typed; ShieldsService rewrites them as eTLD+1 sites.
Strings come from //plainbrowser/shields (AddSettingsStrings, strings in 60-ui/0008), called at the end of
settings::AddLocalizedStrings. The same element holds the toggle for daily filter list updates (Local State pref
plainbrowser.adblock.list_updates.enabled, registered through 20-hooks), also allowlisted; settingsPrivate finds Local State
prefs by itself. Above the list, the global "Block ads and trackers" toggle (plainbrowser.adblock.enabled); below
the update toggle, when the lists were last checked (plainbrowser.adblock.list_updates.last_success) and a link to
chrome://adblock (20-hooks/0003). Under the blocking toggle, the optional filter lists (EasyList Cookie List, Fanboy's
Annoyance List, uBlock filters: plainbrowser.adblock.lists.*, Local State, allowlisted); at the end a link to
chrome://recommended-extensions (20-hooks/0003).
---
